      "text": "Page 41, reading. Do you know how to place an order at a restaurant? What would you say to the server if your meal was cold? Eating out. A table for three, sir? Yes, please. We'd like one with a view, if possible. Not a problem. Does this one suit you? Wonderful. Could we get a glass of juice, please? Certainly. Would everyone like orange juice? That would be nice. Thank you. Here are the juices you ordered. May I take your order now? Yes. I think we all decided on the soup of the day and sandwiches. My wife would like a grilled cheese, and my friend prefers turkey. I'll take a vegetarian sandwich. Here's your first course, sir. Our famous broccoli cheese soup. Excuse me, my soup is cold. Is it possible to warm it up some more? I'm sorry, sir. The cooks must have forgotten to check it. I'll take care of it right away. Thank you. I appreciate your good service. It's my pleasure. Again, I'll be back with your hot soup as soon as possible.",
